@anon.984efe779a4077b66be6415f964eeb42.2153 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [511 x i8] }> <{ [511 x i8] c"Forced use of a certain math class.\0A\0AThis is useful to treat certain symbols as if they were of a different\0Aclass, e.g. to make a symbol behave like a relation. The class of a symbol\0Adefines the way it is laid out, including spacing around it, and how its\0Ascripts are attached by default. Note that the latter can always be\0Aoverridden using [`{limits}`](math.limits) and [`{scripts}`](math.scripts).\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0A#let loves = math.class(\0A  \22relation\22,\0A  sym.suit.heart,\0A)\0A\0A$x loves y and y loves 5$\0A```" }>, align 1
